{"n":7,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.00.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.","body":"---\naddress: 10.11.21.0013\ntitle: common-questions\nstate: draft\ntype: general\n---\n\n## Registry\nformat: 7\n\nR10 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:40): face 00 is the registry, the place that lists the page's faces. Layout is `7` (not given).\n\n- `00.draft` registry: draft because sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.\n- `01.draft` law: draft because sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it. The `question` card type is not in the kernel card-type table (decisions.md C8.9); `7`.\n- `04.draft` user: draft because sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.\n\nR11 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:44): the common questions list. Page number `0013` is `7`: chosen in 0010-0019 (static, R17) to match crates/ask (COMPUTE); the Director has not placed it.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":8,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.01.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it. The `question` card type is not in the kernel card-type table (decisions.md C8.9); `7`.","body":"## what is my name\ntype: question\nforms: what is my name\nanswer: 10.11.21.1001.01.bob\n\nR11 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:44): \"The what is my name will become part of a common questions people ask list. When we see a version of this, it becomes linked as a sentence; it works like brands do.\" `7`: the card fields (`type: question`, `forms`, `answer`) match crates/ask `QuestionCard`; the Director has not given them.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":9,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0013.04.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.","body":"## what is my name\nsource: [01 / what is my name] Bob test, session 2 question; why: docs/spec/DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:44\nwhy: This is how we let the compute solve.\n\nWhen the user asks \"what is my name\", the key words what + my + name match this question, and it points to the bob card, the user's name.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.0013"}
{"n":10,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.00.draft","tail":"draft","reason":"sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.","body":"---\naddress: 10.11.21.1001\ntitle: bob\nstate: draft\ntype: general\n---\n\n## Registry\nformat: 7\n\nR10 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:40): face 00 is the registry, the place that lists the page's faces. Layout is `7` (not given).\n\n- `00.draft` registry: draft because sample fixture for the build, not kernel content; nobody has reviewed it.\n- `01` law: seated; approved-by: build-stage (R2); trial: docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md@ed82086; blob: 5415cef2\n\nR15 (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:62): a brand card on face 01 needs no 04 card, so the `04` face that held the bob and cats whys was removed in kernel pass 3.\n\nR2 seat (DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md:7-9, R20 :78-80): face 01 passed TRIAL-K2 and is seated at the cited blob; this face 00 stays a draft (R14). Where a seat record lives is `7` (QUESTIONS Q34): it is kept here, on the registry line, so the seated face itself is unchanged.","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
{"n":11,"at":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","by":"prima-kernel-seed","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1001.01","approved-by":"build-stage (R2)","trial":"docs/trial/kernel-trial-2.md@ed82086 blob 5415cef2","body":"## bob\ntype: brand\nbrand: bob.001\nforms: Bob\nmeans: the user's name\n\n## cats\ntype: brand\nbrand: cats.001\nforms: cats\nmeans: animals the user likes","proposal":"prima-kernel-seed:10.11.21.1001"}
